---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Live observability — The Relic"
  description="See every agent in your org acting in real time. Intent appears before the verdict."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border-b border-white/5">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-6">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <a href="/" class="text-xl font-bold text-white">The Relic</a>
          <nav class="flex items-center gap-6">
            <a href="/" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Home</a>
            <a href="/live-observability" class="text-sm font-medium text-relic-400">Live</a>
            <a href="/policy-testing" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Policy testing</a>
            <a href="/self-host" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">Self-host</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/therelicai/therelic" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">GitHub</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-relic-400">Live observability</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
          Every agent in your org, acting in real time.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-neutral-400">
          Open the Live view. Every active agent surfaces a lane. As each one
          calls a tool, you see the intent appear — what it wants to do — before
          the policy engine returns its verdict. The verdict overwrites the
          intent within a few hundred milliseconds. You're watching the fleet
          think, not the fleet's after-the-fact log.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why intent-before-verdict matters -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Intent before verdict</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-neutral-400">
          Most audit tools show you what happened. The Relic shows you what's
          about to happen — then what was decided. Two distinct frames, paired
          by sequence number, so an analyst can see the rule fire in real time
          and trace the chain of reasoning.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">1 · Intent</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">Agent wants to do X</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              The runtime emits the IntentEvent the moment a tool call is
              parsed, before the policy engine has even produced a verdict.
              Streamed live to the dashboard.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">2 · Verdict</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">X was allowed / denied</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              Same sequence number, sealed in the trace chain, paired with the
              matched rule. The Live view replaces the intent row in place so
              you see the decision land.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-6">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-relic-400">3 · Forensic</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">Every event is sealed</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">
              IntentEvents extend the HMAC chain the trace audit already
              uses. The platform's verifier can prove the sequence is intact —
              no events inserted, deleted, or reordered.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Standalone mode -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Standalone mode is still standalone</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-neutral-400">
          The streaming flush is opt-in. With no <code class="rounded bg-neutral-800 px-1.5 text-relic-300">RELIC_API_KEY</code> set,
          the runtime writes IntentEvents to the local <code class="rounded bg-neutral-800 px-1.5 text-relic-300">.trtrace</code>
          file and never touches the network. The batch trace push at end-of-run
          remains the durable record. Self-hosted deployments keep every byte
          on their own infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer link back -->
    <section class="border-t border-white/5 py-12">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-neutral-400 hover:text-white">← Back to home</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
